add('prepare','Record the original drive and replacement parts','Keep the engine stopped and transmission neutral. Support the bike securely. Confirm functional rear brake and intact old chain engagement. Record tooth wear/damage and both original sprocket faces against OEM196/394; verify new13T/51T part identities, matching520 non-sealed114-link chain and joining components. Remove the front sprocket cover, keeping the original chain and rear wheel installed.',[196,198,394,54],['Replacement pair and114-link chain identified','Old chain/brake can provide stationary holding'],True)
add('front-release','Release the front nut while the old drive remains assembled','Unfold the old washer tabs clear of the nut flats. Following Nick Dole\'s manual method, have the helper hold the rear brake firmly while you use a correctly fitting socket and hand breaker bar to loosen the front nut. Keep the transmission neutral and both wheels/chain installed. Stop if the chain skips or the bike/support moves. Leave the loosened nut fitted until chain removal.',[196,198],['Old tab released before nut rotation','Nut loosened without chain slip or unstable support'],True,True)
add('chain-remove','Remove the old chain','Raise and securely support the rear wheel. Loosen the axle nut and both adjuster locknuts; turn adjusters inward evenly. Remove the old clip, plate and joining link, then remove the chain from its original guide/slider path. Do not run the engine to move it.',[197,111,112],['Old chain removed; new joining components kept separate'])
add('wheel-remove','Remove the rear wheel','Support the wheel, remove its nut and axle, and retain both pullers and side collars in identified positions. Lower the wheel clear of its caliper/bracket guide. The chain is already removed. Keep brake hydraulics closed and prevent pedal operation while the disc is absent.',[134,136],['Wheel/collars/pullers identified','Brake not operated with disc absent'])
add('wheel-inspect','Check the mounting parts','Inspect axle straightness, wheel/hub, side collars, bearings, brake disc and rear sprocket mating face/hardware. Record damage or looseness; do not straighten a bent axle or reuse a damaged mounting surface.',[136],['Original hub, axle, bearings and brake remain serviceable'],True)
add('rear-remove','Remove the worn rear sprocket','Support the wheel without loading its disc. Record bolt/washer arrangement and sprocket orientation. Hold each bolt while removing its self-locking nut, then remove all six fasteners and the sprocket. Clean the hub mating face.',[136,137],['Six fastener positions accounted for','Clean undamaged mounting face'],True)
add('rear-install','Fit the new51-tooth sprocket','Fit the exact newB2W-25451-00 sprocket in OEM orientation on the clean hub face. Restore correct bolts/washers and matching new self-locking nuts. Tighten the six nuts progressively in a crisscross pattern to42Nm while holding bolt heads. Confirm full face seating.',[137,394],['Correct51T part/orientation','All six nuts42Nm and sprocket fully seated'],True)
add('front-remove','Remove the worn front sprocket','Remove the previously loosened nut and discard the old lock washer. Slide off the old sprocket, keeping the original orientation identified. Inspect output-shaft splines and threads and the sprocket seating area. Damage or leakage needs its separate repair before closure.',[196,198],['Shaft threads/splines and seat serviceable'],True)
add('front-fit','Locate the new13-tooth sprocket','Fit exact9383E-13233 in the orientation shown by OEM196 cross-section. Install the new matching lock washer correctly engaged, then fit the nut by hand to retain the assembly. Leave washer tabs unfolded. Final locking agent, torque and tab folding occur after the new chain and wheel are installed.',[196,198,394],['Correct13T sprocket and new washer located','Final torque remains pending'])
add('wheel-refit','Refit the wheel with the brake correctly located','Grease axle and wheel seal lips with lithium-soap grease. Return each collar to its correct side, lift the wheel with its disc between the pads and locate the complete caliper bracket in the swingarm guide. Install left puller and axle from the left; fit right puller, washer and nut, leaving final tightening for chain adjustment.',[138],['Correct collars/pullers and caliper guide engagement'])
add('chain-install','Join the new chain','Route the matching new114-link chain around both new sprockets and the stock slider/guide. Install its matching joining link and plate with a new matching clip: closed end leads in chain travel direction per OEM198. Confirm clip engagement in both pin grooves and free joint movement. Lubricate chain without contaminating tire or brake.',[54,198],['New114-link chain and matching joint','Clip fully seated and correctly directed'],True)
add('slack','Set measured chain slack','With rear wheel raised and transmission neutral, pull chain upward with about50N above the chain-guide mounting bolt. At the exact OEM111/112 reference, measure chain-guide-to-chain-bottom distance. Adjust both sides equally to50–60mm and seat pullers against swingarm ends.',[111,112,199],['Measured50–60mm and equal adjustment recorded'],True)
add('axle-secure','Secure the rear wheel before brake-reaction torque','Tighten rear axle nut to135Nm and both adjuster locknuts to21Nm. Recheck measured slack. Confirm the caliper bracket is located and pedal now has normal firm braking action with disc installed.',[112,138],['Axle135Nm, locknuts21Nm','Brake operates normally and slack remains correct'],True)
add('front-secure','Torque and mechanically retain the front sprocket','Remove the hand-fitted front nut without disturbing the washer/sprocket. Apply OEM-specified LOCTITE to the nut as shown, recording actual product and its instructions because Yamaha gives no grade/cure time. Refit and tighten to90Nm using the same helper-held rear brake and manual torque reaction, engine off and neutral. Firmly fold the new washer tabs against nut flats only after torque. Keep chain and axle installed and secure throughout.',[196,198],['Front nut90Nm with recorded locking agent','New washer tabs securely against flats'],True,True)
add('cover','Restore the sprocket cover','Refit the cover and tighten its bolts to7Nm. Remove all holding tools, parts and supports that interfere with hand wheel rotation.',[196],['Cover7Nm; no tool remains in drive'])
add('final','Verify the complete new drive','Rotate the wheel by hand through several chain positions. Recheck50–60mm slack, chain tracking, master clip seating/direction, both sprocket mountings and normal rear-brake action. Record new part identities, all torques and final slack. Resolve binding, skipping or misalignment before use; comply with the selected locking-agent instructions before loading the joint.',[111,112,138,198,199],['Both sprockets and chain replaced together','Free movement/alignment, retention and final measurements recorded'],True)
